# .adl-ignore file
# This file specifies which files should not be overwritten during generation operations.
# Files listed here typically contain implementations that users have completed.
#
# Patterns supported:
# - Exact file names: tools/agent_tool.go
# - Wildcards: *.go
# - Directory patterns: tools/*
# - Directories: build/
# - Comments: lines starting with #

tools/echo.go
tools/delay.go
tools/error.go
tools/random_data.go
tools/validate.go
tools/simulate_tool_call.go

# Skill playbooks are hand-authored; the generator only seeds blank
# scaffolds. Protect the whole .agents/skills/ tree so regen never clobbers
# the bodies (or any bundled scripts/templates/resources).
.agents/skills/

# Hand-maintained but kept in sync with the generated template. main.go
# carries a SINGLE deviation from `adl generate` output: it wires
# internal/mock.NewMockLLMClient instead of the generator's default
# OpenAI-compatible client (mock-agent's whole purpose is to run without
# real LLM credentials). It is ignored only because the generated template
# hardcodes server.NewOpenAICompatibleLLMClient with no seam to inject a
# custom client. When bumping the ADL CLI, regenerate into a scratch dir and
# re-apply just that one swap (see the header note in main.go). Dropping this
# entry entirely is blocked on an adl-cli extension point for a custom LLM
# client (tracked upstream) - until then, keeping it synced by hand is how we
# pick up template fixes like the OTel service.name propagation.
main.go

# Hand-authored example stacks (docker-compose, collector configs, docs)
# that live outside the generated surface.
examples/

# Add your own files to ignore here:
# my-custom-file.go
# config/secrets.yaml

